        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Cuckoo',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cuckoo is a card game in which each player is dealt one card and may exchange it with the next player; the aim is to avoid holding the lowest card and losing a life. Last player left in wins. Also known as Chase the Ace and Ranter Go Round (Britain), Screw Your Neighbor (USA).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Country/Region of Origin: England and France. The English variant (Ranter Go Round, Chase the Ace) is a traditional English game, said to have been first played in Cornwall; documented from 1881 (Cassell's). A similar game known as Cuckoo in most European countries originated in 16th-century France and developed into the French game Coucou.\nTime Period: 16th century (France); 19th century (England)\nHistorical Development: French Coucou lineage; English Ranter Go Round described by 1881, with scoring variants (e.g. Professor Hoffmann 1891).\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game in Britain (as Ranter Go Round/Chase the Ace) and USA (as Screw Your Neighbor); Cuckoo group played across Europe.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: Optional',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Standard 52-card deck\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck\nScore sheet (optional)\nTable space',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards per Player: Varies by player count\nDealing Pattern: Clockwise\n--',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
